      "text": "Given the function $y = \\tan x + \\cot x$, we can rewrite it as:\n\n\\[\ny = \\tan x + \\csc x \\cot x = \\frac{1}{\\sin x} \\cdot \\csc x \\cdot \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x \\cdot \\sin x} = \\cot 2x\n\\]\n\nTo find the period, we observe that the function $\\cot 2x$ has a period of $\\pi$, since $\\cot 2(x + \\pi) = \\cot 2x$. Thus, the period of $y = \\tan x + \\cot x$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\pi}\n\\]\n\nOr, if we were to use Python to solve it, we could write a simple script to verify our reasoning.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable and function\nx = sp.symbols('x')\ny = sp.tan(x) + 1/sp.tan(x)\n\n# Simplify the function\ny_simplified = sp.simplify(y)\n\n# Derive the period\nperiod = sp.periodicity(y_simplified, x)\nprint(period)\n```",
